Hi,&nbsp;<br />
<br />
Please find the tax bill for . Please check your HUD/Closing documents. You should have been given money for the time you did not own this property this year.&nbsp;<br />
<br />
If you own this property outright then you are responsible to pay the taxes each year.&nbsp;<br />
<br />
If this property is mortgaged then the taxes should be escrow out of your monthly payments. Taxes will then be paid by the lender.&nbsp;<br />
<br />
Lastly, if this property is in a self directed IRA account then you will most likely need to direct payment for these taxes to be paid.&nbsp;<br />
<br />
I would recommend that you check in with your lender/IRA company to make sure that they will issue payment.&nbsp;<br />
<br />
Just a reminder that Shelby County taxes are considered late on February 28th.&nbsp;<br />
<br />
The county will be updating their records into your name so next year the tax bills will go directly to you, the lender and/or the SDIRA company.&nbsp;<br />
<br />
​Pleas​e let me know if you have further questions.